WEBVTT

1
00:00:05.150 --> 00:00:09.050
After the party and the house cleaning,
<c.hl>trash of every kind</c> piles up!

2
00:00:10.550 --> 00:00:12.890
How on earth should we throw it all out?

3
00:00:16.950 --> 00:00:18.150
<c.hl>Wait!</c>

4
00:00:18.300 --> 00:00:22.600
<c.hl>Chicken bones</c> and <c.hl>hard seeds</c>
can't go in the food waste bag!

5
00:00:22.800 --> 00:00:25.400
Shall we check with the smart <c.hl>QR code</c>?

6
00:00:26.800 --> 00:00:30.750
For food waste,
check the <c.hl>item guide</c> carefully.

7
00:00:31.200 --> 00:00:35.900
<c.note>[On screen] General waste: hard shells and pits,</c>
<c.note>eggshells, bones, clam and crab shells</c>

8
00:00:36.550 --> 00:00:39.370
Banana and tangerine peels are <c.hl>food waste</c>,

9
00:00:40.050 --> 00:00:41.380
but <c.hl>chicken bones</c>,

10
00:00:41.450 --> 00:00:43.080
but chicken bones, <c.hl>hard fruit pits</c>

11
00:00:43.150 --> 00:00:45.630
but chicken bones, hard fruit pits
and pineapple skin are <c.hl>general waste</c>.

12
00:00:52.000 --> 00:00:54.150
<c.hl>Squeeze out the water</c> before disposal.

13
00:00:59.240 --> 00:01:03.000
<c.hl>Rinse</c> milk and other paper cartons
and use the <c.hl>carton bin</c>!

14
00:01:05.750 --> 00:01:10.070
For clear PET bottles, <c.hl>empty them</c>,
<c.hl>remove the label</c>

15
00:01:12.150 --> 00:01:14.420
and <c.hl>crush them</c>. Apart from other plastics,

16
00:01:15.950 --> 00:01:19.600
always put them out <c.hl>separately</c>!
<c.note>[On screen] Cap on, then in a clear bag</c>

17
00:01:22.250 --> 00:01:26.580
Gas canisters <c.hl>can explode</c>,
so don't force holes into them.

18
00:01:27.250 --> 00:01:30.800
<c.hl>Press the nozzle outdoors</c>
to release all the gas.

19
00:01:31.750 --> 00:01:35.400
<c.note>[On screen] Once empty, put it out with cans</c>

20
00:01:35.950 --> 00:01:40.560
So collectors don't get hurt,
wrap broken glass well in <c.hl>thick paper</c>,

21
00:01:40.670 --> 00:01:45.480
then put it in a <c.hl>pay-as-you-throw bag</c>
or a <c.hl>special sack for non-burnable waste</c>.

22
00:01:45.520 --> 00:01:47.910
<c.note>[On screen] ✕ Not in the glass bottle bin</c>

23
00:01:47.950 --> 00:01:51.040
<c.hl>Flushing</c> leftover medicine
or putting it <c.hl>in the trash</c>

24
00:01:51.150 --> 00:01:52.790
pollutes the environment!

25
00:01:53.350 --> 00:01:55.350
Use a <c.hl>community center's medicine bin</c>,

26
00:01:55.650 --> 00:02:01.300
a <c.hl>health center</c>, or a <c.hl>mailbox</c> in Seoul.
<c.note>[On screen] Pills: sealed envelope marked “폐의약품”</c>
<c.note>Liquids: mailbox ✕</c>

27
00:02:01.950 --> 00:02:04.120
Clean clothes go in the <c.hl>clothing bin</c>!

28
00:02:06.350 --> 00:02:09.610
Report blankets as <c.hl>bulky waste</c>
before putting them out.

29
00:02:13.650 --> 00:02:17.730
Large appliances like fridges get
<c.hl>free home pickup, even just one</c>!

30
00:02:18.850 --> 00:02:24.900
Small appliances like fans:
check the <c.hl>quantity rule</c>.
<c.note>[On screen] 5 or more: free pickup</c>
<c.note>(fewer than 5: community center)</c>

31
00:02:25.550 --> 00:02:30.140
Furniture: report it as bulky waste
on the <c.hl>Seodaemun-gu Office website</c>,

32
00:02:32.250 --> 00:02:33.580
<c.hl>pay the fee</c>,

33
00:02:34.550 --> 00:02:36.340
label it with the <c.hl>report number</c>,

34
00:02:37.250 --> 00:02:38.120
Done!

35
00:02:39.200 --> 00:02:41.300
Smart student <c.hl>quiz</c>!

36
00:02:41.500 --> 00:02:49.000
<c.note>[On screen] Leftover medicine down the toilet?</c>
<c.note>Clear PET: label off, put out separately?</c>
<c.note>One large appliance: free pickup?</c>

37
00:02:51.050 --> 00:02:53.240
<c.hl>Putting out clear PET bottles separately</c>

38
00:02:53.350 --> 00:02:55.770
and <c.hl>free pickup for one large appliance</c>

39
00:02:55.850 --> 00:02:57.150
are both <c.hl>correct</c>!

40
00:02:58.150 --> 00:03:00.540
Proper disposal, and <c.hl>our home is spotless</c>!

41
00:03:00.950 --> 00:03:05.150
Got trash to throw out today?
<c.hl>Check once more</c> before you put it out!

42
00:03:06.200 --> 00:03:11.900
<c.note>[On screen] Contact: Seodaemun-gu Office,</c>
<c.note>Sanitation Admin. Division</c>
